{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Tzaphenath Paaneach.</b> If this word is Egyptian, we do not know its meaning, and if it is a translation, we do not know Joseph's name [in Egyptian], and the meaning of paaneach would be as the Aramaic translator translated it, and it [the full name] is a four-letter word." "<b>Priest of On.</b> A servant of HaShem or a servant of idolatry, for \"priest\" throughout all of Scripture means nothing but \"one who serves,\" in my opinion." "<b>And Joseph went out.</b> His name went out, as in the sense of \"your name went out among the nations\" (Ezekiel 16:14). Or he went out and passed through every place, and they proclaimed concerning him, so that they would know him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:46.928631688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}